course: dictionary
lesson: 7082
title: Pavilion: one word, many buildings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pavilion is a kind of building, but the same word can name different buildings. The words around it are the clues that tell you which one. Look at «where a stone marble boat pavilion stands» in the sentence about the Summer Palace.
explain: The clues are Summer Palace (a palace with grounds), stone (the building is solid and made to last), and stands (it sits in one place). So here a pavilion is a decorative building in a garden, not a sports building or a tent. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A small building in the palace grounds fits, but a cricket changing room does not.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right. If it does not, look at the other clues again.
fact: A pavilion is a building.
fact: A cricket pavilion is where players change and rest, and a batter who is out walks back to the pavilion.
fact: At fairs and exhibitions, a pavilion can be a light building or a large tent, and each country may have its own.
fact: In a park or garden, a pavilion is a decorative building for shelter, like a summerhouse.
fact: A hospital can be made up of several pavilions, which are separate buildings joined together as one site.
exercise: In «where a stone marble boat pavilion stands», where is the pavilion? | Under the sea | In a cricket changing room | Inside a sports stadium | *In the grounds of the Summer Palace
exercise: A batter is out and walks back to the pavilion. Where is the pavilion? | In a palace garden, made of stone | *Beside the cricket field, where players change and rest | A hospital ward | A tent at a county fair
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence that tells you the pavilion is made of a solid material. | navy | *stone | debated | rebuild
test: The park had a small pavilion where people sheltered from the rain. What does pavilion mean here? | A cricket ground with bats and stumps | A marble boat in a palace | *A decorative building for shelter, like a summerhouse | A big hall for the navy
test: At a fair, a pavilion can be a large tent. What is the best meaning of pavilion in that place? | A type of boat | A sports changing room | A kind of hospital ward | *A light building or large tent used at a show
exam: Mia says pavilion always means a sports building. Is she right? | Yes, it only ever means a cricket changing room | *No, it can also mean a park shelter or a fair tent, so check the clues | Yes, because pavilion is only a sports word | No, pavilion is a type of fish
